[[34m2026-04-15 08:56:31[0m] fusion_mode='cross_attention'
[[34m2026-04-15 08:56:31[0m]   -> Bidirectional cross-attention between views: each view attends to the other view’s tokens, then features are combined for the rest of the encoder/decoder. Strong when views are aligned but not identical.
[[34m2026-04-15 08:56:31[0m] view_in=2, view_mixing_strategy=embedding
[[34m2026-04-15 08:56:31[0m] use_view_embedding vs use_viewwise_decoder_lora: per-view additive embeddings bias early (or latent) features with a small vector per view; viewwise_decoder_lora adds low-rank adapters on the decoder side conditioned by view index—typically more flexible than a single embedding per view for reconstruction, at the cost of more trainable parameters.
[[34m2026-04-15 08:56:31[0m]   use_view_embedding=False
